# Keep images small, reproducible and free of anything that is not code (rule 14:
# data and runtime state live on VM volumes, never inside an image).
# .git IS included on purpose: `make tdd-check` [G-TDD-01] walks branch history to prove
# the branch was written test-first, so the research/CI image must carry it or the gate goes
# vacuous. The engine and reader images never receive it — their Dockerfiles COPY only
# Cargo manifests and rust/, never `COPY . .` — so no history reaches a production image.
.gitignore
.venv
target/
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
data/
docs/reference/*.docx
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
config/live.yaml
secrets/
